pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% DEFECT: the `conclusion BOUNDS` lower-bound guard compared the claimed bound
% against `best_objective_value`, the objective value of the logged
% representative. `solx` does not remove the representative, it removes the whole
% class of assignments agreeing with it on the preserved variables — here the
% whole x1=0 class, whose minimum is 0 because the objective is over the
% unpreserved x2. The lower bound is then proved *through* the excluding
% constraint: `pol 1 2 +` yields `1 x2 >= 1` and `pol 3 100 *` yields
% `100 x2 >= 100`. The true optimum is 0, witnessed by x1=0, x2=0.
f 1;
solx ~x1 x2;
pol 1 2 +;
pol 3 100 *;
output NONE;
conclusion BOUNDS 100 100 : ~x1 x2;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
